{
  "inShort": "The checkpoint is behind on visible evidence: no playable slice or test report was supplied. The devlog claims five players tested the tide loop, but shows a mountain landscape and a film thumbnail instead. With one week left, two-island sailing, co-op and the test findings remain unverified.",
  "discussed": [
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyivb01awtvz8v6fyg2xh",
      "text": "A public repository of the Godot demo projects the game builds on is supported by the linked repository. It provides examples, licensing and import instructions, not evidence of this game's playable slice."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj2j01axtvz8lc3mdzjj",
      "text": "An animated reference video for the art style remains marked done. The checked title and thumbnail identify Big Buck Bunny. The video was not watched, so its animation and relevance to the chosen style remain unverified."
    },
    {
      "itemId": "cmvuoyj5x01aytvz8lsr5pz2m",
      "text": "A reference article on what playtesting is, for the team to read is supported by Wikipedia's Playtest article. It explains testing methods but does not document the five reported players or their findings."
    }
  ],
  "notDiscussed": [],
  "outsidePlan": [],
  "questions": [
    "Where can the reported playtest document and the build those five players tested be opened?",
    "What did those tests establish about travelling between islands, understanding the tide and sailing together?"
  ],
  "lenses": {
    "marketing": "Devlog #3 reported five testers and received 0 applause and 0 views, but its landscape image and Big Buck Bunny thumbnail show no gameplay, and the project lists no store page or game link.",
    "team": "The stated capacity is 10–15 hours weekly, with Mia's hours unknown. Alex confirmed all three weeks, but Mia stopped confirming after week one, leaving her engineering contribution to co-op sailing unverified.",
    "management": "All four retained tasks are marked done, but they cover references and planning rather than the playable goal due in seven days. The prototype devlog meets the sole stage requirement, yet the supplied evidence establishes neither a working core nor a chosen style for the path toward release."
  }
}

